# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Built binaries -- ROOT-ANCHORED.
# An unanchored "rzp-guard" matches the cmd/rzp-guard/ DIRECTORY too, which
# silently excluded the entire command package from the repository.
/rzp-guard
/rzp-guard.exe

# Build/test scratch
.gotmp/
*.log

# Release artifacts. Reproducible from any commit via ./run.sh release, so
# there is nothing to preserve and a stray stamped binary in the tree invites
# someone to run an unreviewed build.
dist/

# Live-run artifacts (regenerated by ./run.sh)
evidence/live/

# Python reference prototype
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
/gate-verify
/gate-verify.exe
/rzp-study
/rzp-study.exe

# Catch-all for root build artifacts.
#
# The list above was per-binary, so `go build ./...` produced rzp-study.exe,
# `git add -A` committed 10MB of it, and CI's CR check failed on a compiled
# binary being treated as text by the eol=lf default. Enumerating binaries is
# the same whack-a-mole .gitattributes already lost once.
/*.exe
/*.test
/*.out
/rzp-guard-testhook
/rzp-guard-testhook.exe
/rzp-guard-operator
/rzp-guard-operator.exe
/rzp-guard-operator
/rzp-guard-operator.exe
/rzp-guard-operator
/rzp-guard-operator.exe
/rzp-guard-operator-testhook
/rzp-guard-operator-testhook.exe

# State files hold an Argon2id operator verifier. Credential-derived material
# never belongs in a public repo, and this tree is OneDrive-backed (F12).
# Gates write state to an OS temp dir; nothing here needs a committed .db.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Raw provider responses. Committed evidence is a redacted projection
# built by evidence/redact.py; raw records stay local.
evidence/*/raw/
